§ `Tests -- the forms of the charge, the closing words, and provisions the list does not name`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 183 provision of an Act`
`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` MEANS `s 183 provision of the Criminal Code` (`Provision of the Code` OF n , sub)

-- The lead-in: "an offence contrary to, any conspiracy or attempt to commit or being an accessory after the fact in relation to an offence contrary to, or any counselling in relation to an offence contrary to" a listed provision.
#ASSERT `s 183 offence` `the offence itself` (`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` 184 "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 183 offence` `a conspiracy to commit the offence` (`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` 184 "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 183 offence` `an attempt to commit the offence` (`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` 184 "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 183 offence` `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence` (`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` 184 "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 183 offence` `counselling in relation to the offence` (`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` 184 "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a form of participation that is none of the five, on a listed provision: the definition says "means" and the form is outside it
#ASSERT `s 183 offence` `a form of participation that is none of those` (`s 183 test Criminal Code provision` 184 "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

